{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names","id":277637,"title":"Good Shadow Names","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-10T16:01:41-07:00","id":277637,"title":"Good Shadow Names","content":"What are some of the best/most interesting Shadow Names you've seen?<br /> <br /> What factors into your decision to give a character a particular shadow name? If you want to share examples from your own games, please do!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T16:51:37-07:00","id":277682,"title":"","content":"I made a Libertine Obrimos focused on making Phantasms and <i>Imbued Items</i> named Toymaker.<br /> <br /> My brother made a sword using AA Obrimos that went by Damocles.<br /> <br /> Given that Shadow Names are meant to be Meaningful Names I generally try to pick names based on the character's goal, foibles, or stylistic focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T16:58:01-07:00","id":277686,"title":"","content":"I'm currently playing a Moros Guardian detective in an online Mage Noir game. His shadow name is Cerberus.<br /> <br /> (Partly due to the obvious connotations of being a &quot;Guardian&quot; of the dead, and partly from a detail of how I play him that seems to have slipped past the other players; his Unseen Sense is centered around his sinuses, so he tends to sniff whenever something supernatural sets 'em off, making him look a bit like a hound catching a scent.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T20:25:21-07:00","id":277796,"title":"","content":"My chars:<br /> <br /> A Mastigos Bene Ashmedai named Dante Alighieri.<br /> <br /> An Obrimos from the Mysterium that tries to promote wisdom among his peers named Keter<br /> <br /> My ST npcs:<br /> <br /> * totally-nuts-acanthus-archmaster called: &quot;Fourth Doctor&quot;<br /> * the late most advanced Bene Ashmedai called &quot;Baphomet&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll edit with more as soon as I remember some other particularly good ones.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T22:48:50-07:00","id":277897,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of names that appear normal (or no-too-far-outt nicknames) but have symbolic significance<br /> <br /> The 'crazy' homeless Thyrsus called Thomas Bethlehem, referencing Tom o'Bedlam<br /> The serial killer Mastigos called Bluejay (which is linked to the devil in Deep South folklore)<br /> The quiet Moros thanotologist named Romero (both a reference to the director and linking to the name Romero meaning 'a pilgrim to/guardian of graveyards')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T12:25:05-07:00","id":278295,"title":"","content":"I had a mentor Arrow NPC named Ronin. <i>His </i>mentor was the previous Adamant Sage, who started a very violent shadow war with the Seer pylon in town, and whose ensuing Ascension gambit drew so much Exarch attention that the Guardians hired another Arrow Caucus to kill him before he could doom the entire Pentacle. They ended up surrounding and cutting down the Sage and all his apprentices, save one, who threw himself into the Underworld after seeing his master's body.<br /> <br /> A year later, he was discovered brooding in a cemetery by the Hierarch that had been appointed to the thankless task of restoring order. She didn't recognize him, but could tell he was a seasoned warrior, and so appointed him a Sentinel. When she asked his name, he told her that he had lost his Name when he had lost his family, and that now he was only Ronin. He quietly carries out his duties to the Consilium, glowering inwardly at the new Arrow Caucus that has moved into the area and waiting for the day he can find a worthy apprentice and begin to redeem himself...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:42:21-07:00","id":279671,"title":"","content":"The best shadow name I have ever heard was for a free council, 1940's, mob boss that had resources 5, more goons than you can shake a stick at, and his own freakin' casino in Portland! The mage's shadow name was &quot;Mr. Cash.&quot; I can't take credit for this one though, my friend in the game played this PC and I LOVED interacting with him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T19:13:44-07:00","id":280412,"title":"","content":"Once had a Time/Matter-focused NPC named &quot;Little Clock&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T22:11:49-07:00","id":280610,"title":"","content":"A Keeper of the Covenant named &quot;Arbiter.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:14:17-07:00","id":281020,"title":"","content":"A Moros Alchemist named &quot;Engy&quot; (TF2), an Acanthus Guardian called &quot;Taokaka&quot; (BlazBlue), an Obrimos AA Sentinel called &quot;Leonidas&quot; (no, not the movie one), a Guardians Mastigos Matriarch called Helen (as in, &quot;of Troy&quot;). An Acanthus hacker called Hash.<br /> <br /> I reckon videogame character names (as well as movies, litterature, history, etc.) used as Shadow names mustn't be uncommon, especially amongst younger Mages that want to emulate their idols or favorites, or just mages that want to evoke a specific theme or inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:23:08-07:00","id":281031,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've been the ST of many a Mage campaign, so I have a few lying around. I'll list a few of my favourites<br /> <br /> Fafnir, the Mastigos Mysterium censor was someone I liked.<br /> Leviathan, a Scelestus, whose path eludes me.<br /> Themistocles, Adamantine Arrow, of course. Thyrsus or Obrimos<br /> An archmage with three distinct personalities, all named after one of the sons of Noah; Shem, Ham and Japheth.<br /> <br /> And finally, a Mastigos Apostate who went by the name of The Walking Man. Who was a rather creepy kind of guy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, most of my mages have taken names they think fit them, or their goals. More than a few have taken names to intimidate their enemies, political and regular alike.<br /> Most of all, however, I want names that are kind of memorable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:35:49-07:00","id":281242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=280610#post280610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Keeper of the Covenant named &quot;Arbiter.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And now I have that song stuck in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:46:31-07:00","id":281499,"title":"","content":"One of my players' Cabals relied completely on angelic imagery and each was names after the four Archangels (Michael the Obrimos, Uriel the Moros, Raphael the Thyrsus, and Gabriel the Acanthus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T18:35:34-07:00","id":283023,"title":"","content":"I'm currently playing a Bearer of the Eternal Voice by the name of Iago. As if being a Guardian and a Whisperer wasn't enough to make people distrustful, the reactions I got from players familiar with the plot of Othello were absolutely priceless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","user":"Cardran","date":". 10-15-2014, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T05:50:46-07:00","id":283765,"title":"","content":"I only play a Mastigos hacker, freelance designer from the Free Council. He\u00b4s named &quot;Janus&quot;. He actually is figuring out his own name...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T08:29:52-07:00","id":286632,"title":"","content":"Since the character just came to mind in another thread...<br /> <br /> Thanatos - A GotV Moros Interfector who believed himself to be (and was slated to eventually become, because yay ascension!) the concept of peaceful death. Assassin, carnifex, and general all-around troubleshooter. I miss playing him so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T09:33:54-07:00","id":286686,"title":"","content":"I just remembered another character from one of my games (inspired by the earlier chronicle I mentioned with the archangel names) similar your character Raikirah:<br /> Azrael, Archmaster of Life and Death. His goal was to help the souls of the world find peace, challenging the Exarch's lie that Death is an end and should be feared. He has spent over a millenia working to this end, and counts himself a member of the Bodhissatvas. <br /> <br /> He was a fun NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T12:26:11-07:00","id":687389,"title":"","content":"Little topic necormancy - <b>I need Shadow Names for the at least one Sentinel for the story I will run</b> - and I do not have any idea where to look them up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They all are coming from the London's City leading cabal <i><b>Visus Urbem</b> </i>( Eyes of City ), from what are Hierarch Civitas and his Provost Decurion. The Sentinels ideas are Mastigos of Adamantine Arrow, Thyrsus from Guardians, and Obrimos of Silver Ladder. Other details are not set in stone, and even those are more guidlinies. Still, ladies would be more appreciated, as there are enought male characters in the cabal.<br /> <br /> Part of the cabal was also <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/677451-badges-of-power-how-officers-of-consilium-confirms-their-legal-jurisdiction?p=677662#post677662\">Obrimos of Guardians street-preacher called <b>Fallen King</b></a>, but he clashed with Civitas, and left cabal to be Solitarie - even if he is still Herald of the city and Legacy student under Decurion, also still working on good terms with Ruling Council.<br /> <br /> <b>Seeing as both Civitas and Decurion are Latin terms, maybe Shadow Names of cabal-mates would also be?</b> Even if yes, where to look for good Names ideas for them? But still, I broke with Fallen King naming convention, so maybe I would make it for the rest of Sentinels? Any ideas on topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-03-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T12:48:09-07:00","id":687408,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the names of Civitas cabalmates be in the London book?<br /> <br /> If they're not in the same cabal then break the naming convention. Anyways, just their Path and Order aren't enough to think up good shadow names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T17:12:33-07:00","id":687623,"title":"","content":"I've played or made...<br /> Indigo, Acanthus AA, named after the color of her nimbus.<br /> Kali, Moros AA, named after the Indian goddess, of course.<br /> Jordan, Obrimos AA, Steward of the Celestial Orrery, named after the river, the site of one of Jesus' miracles (his sister was named Cana).<br /> Jude, Acanthus AA, House of Ariadne, named after St Jude, the patron saint of the Chicago Police department.<br /> Vale, Moros AA, named for the word because of its homophonic meanings.<br /> Raze, Mastigos GoV, undercover AA, Fang of Mara, named for his penchant for breaking things, objects, people.<br /> <br /> And too many NPCs to count, each named for whatever purpose they would serve in the story: mentors, politicians, antagonists, stuff like that. So, a PC was named Phobos, so his NPC Mentor was named Mars, stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T20:51:57-07:00","id":687842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=687389#post687389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little topic necormancy - <b>I need Shadow Names for the at least one Sentinel for the story I will run</b> - and I do not have any idea where to look them up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They all are coming from the London's City leading cabal <i><b>Visus Urbem</b> </i>( Eyes of City ), from what are Hierarch Civitas and his Provost Decurion. The Sentinels ideas are Mastigos of Adamantine Arrow, Thyrsus from Guardians, and Obrimos of Silver Ladder. Other details are not set in stone, and even those are more guidlinies. Still, ladies would be more appreciated, as there are enought male characters in the cabal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright Wyrd, sounds like you need a Mastigos Arrow, a Guardian Thyrsus, and an Obrimos Thearch, right? I've got one of those for you that I made up for a chronicle of my own (set in DC) who you might find to be rather entertaining in a London setting.<br /> <br /> Duke(Arrow Mastigos) is an awfully loud and impolite American military contractor. It's hard to imagine he's been as temperamental and quick to yell his whole life, or he would have surely ruptured an artery by now. It's not clear to most London mages if he named himself after the University (whose mascot would be appropriate for the Mastigos) or if he obnoxiously pretends to royalty, or, some chortle, he named himself after the character in the American children's cartoon, &quot;GI Joe.&quot; Those who know him a bit better know he sees the whole world as a battlefield in chaos, in need of someone to start shouting commands; in need of a <i>dux</i>. (You could probably also make Duke a woman, in which case the fact her name isn't &quot;Duchess&quot; makes it even more apparent upon investigation that the name is about the origin of the noble title, and not the noble title itself.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T23:03:20-07:00","id":687965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=687842#post687842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright Wyrd, sounds like you need a Mastigos Arrow, a Guardian Thyrsus, and an Obrimos Thearch, right? I've got one of those for you that I made up for a chronicle of my own (set in DC) who you might find to be rather entertaining in a London setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, at least for now. They are raught guidlines for now, but I was trying to make unconvenional characters of their Path/Orders combination. I think that maybe better to this would be Moros Thearch in the end, but maybe this combo will be hard to make in to Sentinel idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=687842#post687842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duke(Arrow Mastigos) is an awfully loud and impolite American military contractor. It's hard to imagine he's been as temperamental and quick to yell his whole life, or he would have surely ruptured an artery by now. It's not clear to most London mages if he named himself after the University (whose mascot would be appropriate for the Mastigos) or if he obnoxiously pretends to royalty, or, some chortle, he named himself after the character in the American children's cartoon, &quot;GI Joe.&quot; Those who know him a bit better know he sees the whole world as a battlefield in chaos, in need of someone to start shouting commands; in need of a <i>dux</i>. (You could probably also make Duke a woman, in which case the fact her name isn't &quot;Duchess&quot; makes it even more apparent upon investigation that the name is about the origin of the noble title, and not the noble title itself.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting NPC, I may steal him to the game - with sex change twist. But I rather strive to &quot;non-warrior&quot; Arrows, as to break stereotypes that all Arrows are paramiliatry guys. For example, we have assasin Moros Arrow <i>Argus Panoptes</i> ( that is PC and exGuardian ), &quot;Doctor Strange wannabe&quot; <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BackAlleyDoctor\" target=\"_blank\">back alley surgeon</a> Obrimos Arrow <i>Doctor Weird</i> and Thyrsus Arrow modern knight <i>Sir Gawain</i> ( memeber of mine <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/92189-european-knight-legacy?p=95253#post95253\"><b>Order of Round Table</b> Legacy</a>, Solitare Sentinel to Consilum ). The Adamant Sage is <i>Hesiesh</i>, Obrimos Tamer of Fire that is veteran of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falklands_War\" target=\"_blank\">Falklands War</a>. We even have a young Obrimos Arrow <i>Padawan</i> that firmly believe she is Jedi-in-training. ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jedi_census_phenomenon#England_and_Wales\" target=\"_blank\">Jediisim is 7th major religion in UK</a>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> With that I would rather not use military contactor as charcter concept, wanting to break &quot;warrior archetypes&quot; in Arrows - <b><i>it's one of problems I have with Adamintine Arrow Order at large</i></b> - it's hard to think character for it that in not direct &quot;warrior&quot; in their Sleeper lives. This is why I loved so much <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=675013#post675013\"><b>Sorcerer Supreme</b> animated movie</a>, as pointing that neurosurgeon is great Arrow character concept.<br /> <br /> Now thinking about it maybe I would use Scotland Yard detective that see minds of psychopaths as forest in Sympathy forest that he need to point to, like Professor X with his Cerebro. But still, it's paramilitary organisation, even if character is not so much focused on combat himself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> On the other hand, police officer is very much in tune with <b><i>Visus Urbem</i></b> general theme of &quot;watchers of London&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hmm, maybe then steal other half of Doctor Strange background and make neurosurgeon Arrow that dwells in to psyche of humans? Or use <b>DaveB</b>'s from the DC character <i>Mara</i> as example Arrow - psychologist that try to help Sleepers and Awakened to cope with trauma? But those do not sound as Sentinels ideas...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=687408#post687408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the names of Civitas cabalmates be in the London book?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are not. Only character connected to Hierach<i> Civitas </i>mentioned in book <b>Shadows of UK</b> is <i>Decurion</i>, his Provost. Whole book is <b><i>very</i></b> sparse on setting, that's why it's so big problem to make it - note here, note there. Sometimes I thought that totally unconnected setting could be better. But I run with what I have and wait for 2ED corebook and it's London description to make large changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=687408#post687408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're not in the same cabal then break the naming convention.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are from the same cabal - made by me <i><b>Visus Urbem</b></i>. It's most politically dedicated cabal in setting, and unofficial Hierarch's <i>Civitas</i> lapdogs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=687408#post687408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, just their Path and Order aren't enough to think up good shadow names.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I pointed many times - I strive to run London as rather very traditional Consilium, with pointing that it has a little paranoia to the Veil policy, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/620130-jonathan-strange-mr-norrell-as-awakening-game#post620130\">started from Britain's Witch Trials</a>. Till 2 years ago whole of it was made almost <b>only</b> from Diamond Order, Free Council was mostly foreigns and migrants to &quot;old, white London&quot;. Situation changed after mass strikes under the Ruling Council offices that almost ended with breaching the Veil - and by this, Libertines Strategos, Arabic <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pir_(Sufism)\" target=\"_blank\">Pir</a> Thyrsus Dreamspeaker <i>Afaza</i>, could join Ruling Council. Still, if character is sounding as something from &quot;old&quot; or &quot;British magic&quot; it surely works for the mine version of London setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2015, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T23:04:51-07:00","id":687966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=687389#post687389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little topic necormancy - <b>I need Shadow Names for the at least one Sentinel for the story I will run</b> - and I do not have any idea where to look them up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They all are coming from the London's City leading cabal <i><b>Visus Urbem</b> </i>( Eyes of City ), from what are Hierarch Civitas and his Provost Decurion. The Sentinels ideas are Mastigos of Adamantine Arrow, Thyrsus from Guardians, and Obrimos of Silver Ladder. Other details are not set in stone, and even those are more guidlinies. Still, ladies would be more appreciated, as there are enought male characters in the cabal.<br /> <br /> Part of the cabal was also <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/677451-badges-of-power-how-officers-of-consilium-confirms-their-legal-jurisdiction?p=677662#post677662\">Obrimos of Guardians street-preacher called <b>Fallen King</b></a>, but he clashed with Civitas, and left cabal to be Solitarie - even if he is still Herald of the city and Legacy student under Decurion, also still working on good terms with Ruling Council.<br /> <br /> <b>Seeing as both Civitas and Decurion are Latin terms, maybe Shadow Names of cabal-mates would also be?</b> Even if yes, where to look for good Names ideas for them? But still, I broke with Fallen King naming convention, so maybe I would make it for the rest of Sentinels? Any ideas on topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always liked the name Karait for a Thyrsus Guardian... maybe a Subtle One?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T08:54:18-07:00","id":688390,"title":"","content":"I mule more on the Sentinels idea and I would probably go with Scotland Yard detective that is Mastigos Arrow in the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/legacies/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Eleventh Question</b> Legacy</a>. Yes, Questions are Mysterium and Guardians Legacy, but I feel that this kind of &quot;serial killer hunter&quot; cop Arrow would be very suited for it - and 2ED rules ( shown in linked spoiler blog ) shows characters outside of Legacies Parental Path and Order can join those communities. Any good ideas for his Shadow Name?<br /> <br /> As he will be &quot;serial killers/Mad hunter&quot; I think that some connections to Jack the Ripper case - as most famous serial killer case in London - are totally in order. ( Especially for Mastigos, with &quot;From Hell&quot; letters. ) Calling him <i>Jack</i> will be ill suited, but maybe <b><i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_the_Ripper#Investigation\" target=\"_blank\">Abberline</a></i> </b>will be good Shadow Name for him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2015, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:16:15-07:00","id":688491,"title":"","content":"Whitechapel might be another one. Or Vigilance, pulled from the group there of the same name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:24:58-07:00","id":688501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=688491#post688491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whitechapel might be another one. Or Vigilance, pulled from the group there of the same name.</div> </div> </div> </div>They sound rather as cabals, but I will have them as alternatives, just in case. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:25:36-07:00","id":688502,"title":"","content":"My favorite that I've used is Harlaquinn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T14:15:35-07:00","id":688760,"title":"","content":"Not really had chance to use much yet, but my favourite idea so far: an Obrimos whose Awakening involved perceiving the Aether and everything in it as harmonious sound - and that includes himself. Big Music of the Spheres theme. If I play him, he'll introduce himself thus: &quot;My name is Song.&quot;<br /> <br /> The elegant simplicity of that one is largely down to the fact that I wouldn't be giving him the scientific and mathematical side of the Obrimos path, because if he knew pure maths I'd be unable to resist the hideous bilingual pun of calling him Cantor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T15:03:15-07:00","id":688836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=688760#post688760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really had chance to use much yet, but my favourite idea so far: an Obrimos whose Awakening involved perceiving the Aether and everything in it as harmonious sound - and that includes himself. Big Music of the Spheres theme. If I play him, he'll introduce himself thus: &quot;My name is Song.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://www.doctorwhotv.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/series5riversong.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Hello, Sweetie!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I needed to done this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T15:34:49-07:00","id":688933,"title":"","content":"Napoleon, Aristotle, Alexander, Newton, Nietzsche, Cromwell, Poe, Voltaire, Constantine, Augustine, Cicero, Descartes, Roc, Rooster, pilgrim, mangled, auroch, Quetzalcoatl.... basically any historical figure not primarily known for genocide, any mythalogical creature, any god from non-modern religion, any myths, authrian legend <br /> <br /> The key to a good name is to pair the name to the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T23:32:22-07:00","id":689367,"title":"","content":"Fallen - a Mastigos who awakened at the age of 13 during the &quot;emo&quot; period, which resulted in getting over it. Was supposed to be ironic but no one seems to understand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T11:50:12-07:00","id":689960,"title":"","content":"I had a character who's life was destroyed by being accused of committing a murder he had nothing to do with. After faking his own death, he came back with a major vengeance and took the name &quot;Benjamin Barker&quot;. ((if you don't know the name, it was the real name of Sweeney Todd))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T16:49:46-07:00","id":690603,"title":"","content":"I have a player who is an Acanthus in my mage Noir game. She is an orphaned African American Jazz player who also is a lesbian, who has gone through nearly all the difficulties one would expect for such a person in the 1940s (the player does an amazing job though avoiding stereotyping her). She goes by Cadence, specifically based on how it is used in Jazz, so as to signal a transition that follows cause/effect (i.e it is dependent on the prior section, and acts as the bridge that both allows other musicians to see the coming change and identify the shifting melody/rhythm that will define the next segment... which she is how she sees her magic). The reason she chose said. American is not only due to it reflecting her view of magic, but also because in Jazz, a Cadence is also known as a Turnaround, which is how she saw her Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T17:36:17-07:00","id":691815,"title":"","content":"Some of my characters:<br /> <br /> An Acanthus Guardian who plays up the &quot;dumb blonde&quot; image to avoid suspicion. She picked her Shadow Name the same way I picked it for her--she googled &quot;words for pink in other languages&quot; and picked the one that sounded prettiest. So she goes by Ruzicasta.<br /> <br /> A disgraced politician who resigned from office after a sex scandal. Took his namesake from a Roman senator who overthrew a corrupt emperor -- Valerius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T18:32:10-07:00","id":691872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=688760#post688760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really had chance to use much yet, but my favourite idea so far: an Obrimos whose Awakening involved perceiving the Aether and everything in it as harmonious sound - and that includes himself. Big Music of the Spheres theme. If I play him, he'll introduce himself thus: &quot;My name is Song.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a similar character that chose the name Logos, as in the Word of God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T00:31:53-07:00","id":692117,"title":"","content":"I need a help with mine Sentinel idea - I want to make Moros Silver Ladder that would be female member of <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Stygian Heralds</i> ( from <b>Summoners</b> ). She would summon great heroes of the past to invoke Lex Magica retribution.<br /> <br /> Any ideas on Shadow Name you got fro this NPC concept? Best would be somehow connected with London.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T00:43:55-07:00","id":692118,"title":"","content":"How about Clarion, as in the instrument that calls soldiers to war? Or maybe Toll, as in ask not for whom the bell? If you want to tap into Arthurian legend, maybe Nimue, she who granted Arthur his legendary blade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T05:03:36-07:00","id":692253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to tap into Arthurian legend, maybe Nimue, she who granted Arthur his legendary blade? </div> </div> </div>She also takes Arthur off to Avalon. That's a pretty interesting parrallel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T05:39:21-07:00","id":692297,"title":"","content":"Were not Nimue a river nymph? This would indicate more Acanthus name...<br /> <br /> But yes, conceptually she sounds like Sentinel character I have in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T06:28:10-07:00","id":692366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Were not Nimue a river nymph? </div> </div> </div>She's still the ruler of a sort of pseudo-afterlife. There's a mixture of imagary there, it could work for either path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:42:22-07:00","id":692767,"title":"","content":"I will go with Nimue, as Toll and Clarion sound a bit silly in Polish ( like modern English Bell and Horn ).<br /> <br /> The last Sentinel from <b>Visus Urbem</b> cabal I have in my mind would be female Thyrsus from Guardians of Veil. But I cannot decide on Legacy for her - I look in to <i>Orphans of Proteus</i> ( very cool and especially good for Guardians Suspector or Consilium Sentinel, but not very much &quot;city connected&quot; ), <i>Subtle Ones</i> ( Guardian Epopt of mine London is one and maybe interesting would be to have Thyrsus member bent on deciphering &quot;will of London&quot; as it's one organism, but her Mind Attainment would only doable they Life Arcanum possibilities ) or <i>Sodality of Tor</i> ( but I have one Thyrsus Guardian in Ruling Council as one of Tor and I do not see this as very useful Legacy for the Sentinel ). <br /> <br /> Maybe your Shadow Names ideas on those three concepts will help me decide. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:44:20-07:00","id":692768,"title":"","content":"How about Boudicai, she once razed London as retribution for their crimes against her family and people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:52:01-07:00","id":692774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=692768#post692768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Boudicai, she once razed London as retribution for their crimes against her family and people.</div> </div> </div> </div>To what idea you would pin point Boudicai? As I do not see clear analogy in any of concepts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T12:24:51-07:00","id":692818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=692767#post692767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will go with Nimue, as Toll and Clarion sound a bit silly in Polish ( like modern English Bell and Horn ).</div> </div> </div> </div>brb, naming a Free Councillor Bell (more name puns, combining the thing that goes 'ding' with the guy who invented the telephone)<br /> <br /> I could probably do something with Horn if I really tried - maybe riffing off &quot;in the horns of a dilemma.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Not saying your reason for choosing that way is wrong, just taking inspiration from it. :-D )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T15:45:04-07:00","id":693038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=692767#post692767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will go with Nimue, as Toll and Clarion sound a bit silly in Polish ( like modern English Bell and Horn ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to add: if there is ever a name that sounds odd /not appropriate as a Shadow Name in your native language, despite the concept working, you can always use the Latin, Greek, Persian or Hindi words, since those languagea are the basis of many of the Orders terminology. Latin especially works for western mages, as it still forms the basis of legal, medical and scientific terminology across most fields. <br /> <br /> So &quot;horn&quot; becomes &quot;Cornu&quot; if you go with Latin, &quot;S\u012b\u1e45ga&quot; in Hindi, &quot;K\u00f3rna&quot; in Greek and ... well, Google translate didn't help me with Persian. <br /> <br /> Also, people of certain cultural/ethnic background could use their native tongues. Two of my players are playing Irish immigrants in the 1940s, and they use bastardized* Irish Gaelic to come up with their Shadow Names.<br /> <br /> That all said, I like those options you came up with. I just don't want you to feel they have to translate always into Polish <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> *I say bastardized because:<br /> 1. They are playing their characters as people with little education from a nation where Gaelic was banned for huge swaths of time and<br /> 2. Neither speak Gaelic in real life, and it is difficult language to learn with tons of dialects in Ireland alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T17:15:30-07:00","id":693155,"title":"","content":"Do you have more details about the Thyrsus Guardian? Because there are a ton of Thyrsus or Life/Spirit primary legaciesi could fit into such a broad category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T23:01:57-07:00","id":693498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=692774#post692774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To what idea you would pin point Boudicai? As I do not see clear analogy in any of concepts...</div> </div> </div> </div> The London she was razing was the Roman one (outsiders) and she did it in retribution for their abuses (in her eyes, crimes) against the native people of England. Her actions are retribution taken to the extreme, giving it the weight of threat, and she is very much a figure associated with\u200b London. Given the description I've read of Civitas (and that the 'Axe' is already taken) such a figure would seem appropriate. Or you could just name your sentinel the 'Tower of London'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T00:21:13-07:00","id":693519,"title":"","content":"Or Bridges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T00:28:42-07:00","id":693525,"title":"","content":"<b>2ptTakrill</b>, great explanation for Shadow Name. And the Tower of London will go to other Sentinel, outside of <i>Visus Urbem</i> cabal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=693155#post693155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have more details about the Thyrsus Guardian? Because there are a ton of Thyrsus or Life/Spirit primary legaciesi could fit into such a broad category.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've pointed general ideas for Thyrsus Guardian Sentinel I have in previous post...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=692767#post692767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last Sentinel from <b>Visus Urbem</b> cabal I have in my mind would be female Thyrsus from Guardians of Veil. But I cannot decide on Legacy for her - I look in to <i>Orphans of Proteus</i> ( very cool and especially good for Guardians Suspector or Consilium Sentinel, but not very much &quot;city connected&quot; ), <i>Subtle Ones</i> ( Guardian Epopt of mine London is one and maybe interesting would be to have Thyrsus member bent on deciphering &quot;will of London&quot; as it's one organism, but her Mind Attainment would only doable they Life Arcanum possibilities ) or <i>Sodality of Tor</i> ( but I have one Thyrsus Guardian in Ruling Council as one of Tor and I do not see this as very useful Legacy for the Sentinel ).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T01:02:58-07:00","id":693541,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's just a bunch of legacies you rejected. It tells me nothing about her as a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T01:39:28-07:00","id":693553,"title":"","content":"No, i pointed to the three Legacies - but I even limit the dilemma between <i>Orphans of Proteus</i> and <i>Subtle Ones</i>, as they are more cool ideas in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T01:52:37-07:00","id":693562,"title":"","content":"So you want to use one of those legacies but can't pick which? Figure out her personal philosophy and goals and then pick the legacy that meshes best with that.<br /> <br /> You could just pick a legacy, say she thought she would like it, but it turns out she doesn't. <br /> <br /> Or the hero with horrible powers, wants to do good, but got tricked into a heretic legacy.<br /> <br /> If you're this indecisive it could give you the chance to explore the consequences of something as permanent as a legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-08-2015, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T02:02:58-07:00","id":693564,"title":"","content":"I choose <b><i>Subtle Ones</i></b> - they can make interesting Thrysus Guardian - and their relation with <i>Husni</i>, Acanthus Guardian Epopt in <i>Civitas</i> Hierarch cabal could be very interesting political stand point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T00:18:23-07:00","id":694613,"title":"","content":"Thinking more about it, in the end I will go with<i> Boudica</i> as Thyrsus Guardian Sentinel from <i>Orphans of Proteus</i> as it's a bit exotic combination and will have much more sens in the plot idea I have in mind ( especially as she would be lot weaker in Mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> I also work on to independent Sentinels leader after your advice - the Moros called <i>Tower ( of London )</i>, taking Shadow Name after famous prison, she is dedicated to imprisonment of enemies for the Consilium. I still did not decide her Order and Legacy - she could be Adamantine Arrow or Guardians of the Veil, obviously - what would work better to the sorceress embodying concept of Britain's Greatest Prison? As for the Legacy I think about mine fan <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/92189-european-knight-legacy?p=95253#post95253\"><i>Order of the Round Table</i></a> as it is Space based, but maybe you have other idea working with concept on mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T00:50:12-07:00","id":694641,"title":"","content":"There's a Guardian legacy for being a guard of a person, place or thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T00:08:57-07:00","id":695810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=693038#post693038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to add: if there is ever a name that sounds odd /not appropriate as a Shadow Name in your native language, despite the concept working, you can always use the Latin, Greek, Persian or Hindi words, since those languagea are the basis of many of the Orders terminology. Latin especially works for western mages, as it still forms the basis of legal, medical and scientific terminology across most fields.<br /> (...)<br /> Also, people of certain cultural/ethnic background could use their native tongues. Two of my players are playing Irish immigrants in the 1940s, and they use bastardized* Irish Gaelic to come up with their Shadow Names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for this advice - I forget sometimes that Order were created from Hellenistic exchange with India's culture. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Indian names can be especially prominent in Britain, as it was one of greatest colonies of British Empire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's very good idea to translate working simple terms to exotic languages.<br /> <br /> I will go with<i> Nimue</i> here, only because I think there is interesting clash on the <i>Order of Round Table</i> mania on Arthurian Myth and this character being especially <b>not</b> from this group. It will makes nice spice with one of other Sentinel NPCs, <i>Sir Gawain</i> and <i>Tower ( of London )</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-10-2015, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T00:44:38-07:00","id":695843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=694641#post694641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Guardian legacy for being a guard of a person, place or thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I checked and Attainments from <i>Votaries of the Ordained</i> does sound a bit weak - Superlative luck here, Curses there. In comparing to mine <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/92189-european-knight-legacy?p=95253#post95253\">Order of Round Table</a>, where you can summon your weapons and armor, cast magic in many places at once ( looking over few prison chambers ) and even creating your own Pocket Realm jail. I think it works much better as embodiment of &quot;The Prison&quot; idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-10-2015, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T23:06:49-08:00","id":795414,"title":"","content":"I had a con-man Mastigos named &quot;Sawyer&quot;.(a reference to both the TV show &quot;Lost&quot;, and the song by &quot;Rush&quot;)<br /> \u200bI also had a Matter/crafting focused Moros named &quot;Smith&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T00:36:47-08:00","id":795454,"title":"","content":"I have a Moros 11th Question called Keats. He wanted to be a writer, then after Awakening realized he could never write anything meaningful again that could be shown to Sleepers for fear of subconsciously slipping Supernal truths on it, and thus limits himself to writing only shallow meaningless drivel. He solves crimes to pass the time and avoid writing at all if he can.<br /> <br /> Other characters with good names from my players:<br /> <br /> 23: An Acanthus FC that saw the number 23 everywhere (it was his Unseen Sense reaction).<br /> Herod: Sent to assasinate the leader of a cult that was being manipulated by an Abyssal thing (this is based on a real-life cult in northern Mexico called Fidencistas, their leaders style themselves in the image of the Ni\u00f1o Fidencio, which was in turn a kid which hosted supposed reincarnation of Christ and remained a child all his life while working miracles).<br /> Zakariya Al'Razi: A young FC self-styled Alchemist.<br /> Jakobson: A young FC Obrimos Crypotologos with an obsession for linguistics.<br /> Ozymandias: A SL Sisterhood of the Blessed owner of the once most important Hallow in the city, leader of a critical cabal. Everything fell apart eventually.<br /> Tzitzimime: A SL Mastigos hierarch, young and inexperienced though.<br /> Astarte: A FC Mastigos girl from Russia that always worn horns and looked crazy but inoffensive, eventually turned out to be a banisher from the start. Managed to get the FC of the city to eat the flesh of a Mage she killed by slipping parts of it into the meals while pegging her crimes on the Seers.<br /> Marquis of O: A Mastigos SL with a sadistic bent and member of the Reality Stalkers, always dressed in 100% red clothing.<br /> Persephone: An Arrow which Seers predicted would become the host of an Ochema of the Unity. In her attempts to prevent her fate she became infested by Abyssal entities and things went downhill from there.<br /> <br /> Others from NPCs:<br /> <br /> The Adversary: A Mastigos Councilor that does his best to antagonize literally everyone just to cause them existential doubt.<br /> Mr. X and Ms. Y: A couple of Seers with powerful influence over one of the police precincts in the city.<br /> Adramelech: A Mastigos Reaper which devised an operation that could make kids under 12 yo permanently incapable of evil acts.<br /> Iscariot: An ex-SL Obrimos which believes he can ascend through embodiment of the concept of Redemption through Treason.<br /> The Monitor: A Seer from Panopticon which some think can communicate with her selves from other realities (literally from other chronicles where she appears).<br /> Acteon: A sleepwalker politician (yes, he knows that he needs a shadow name despite not being a mage and despite him being a public persona) that actively seeks mages to work for them in exchange for boons. Mages who cross him have a bad time.<br /> Joe Wasp: World renowned fashion designer by day, high-ranking Praetorian dealing in weapons trafficking by night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","user":"arthexis","date":". 12-30-2015, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T03:08:58-08:00","id":796558,"title":"","content":"McGruff the eleventh question guardian of the veil.<br /> <br /> He was trapped in form of a dog in his younger years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T04:48:41-08:00","id":796778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=795414#post795414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a con-man Mastigos named &quot;Sawyer&quot;.(a reference to both the TV show &quot;Lost&quot;, and the song by &quot;Rush&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>And not a reference to Tom Sawyer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T04:58:22-08:00","id":796784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Adversary: A Mastigos Councilor that does his best to antagonize literally everyone just to cause them existential doubt. </div> </div> </div>Does it work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T05:53:23-08:00","id":796792,"title":"","content":"A character I played<br /> Kuma Lisa, A slightly jerk-ass trickster she would just introduce herself as &quot;Lisa&quot; with &quot;Kuma&quot; as a second name So it wasn't immediately obvious that she was using a shadow name and she'd pretend she didn't know what a shadow name was and lisa was her birth name just to spook out the paranoid mages around her, Only if someone had a good background knowledge on folktales or had the sense to put her name into a search engine they'd realize that she was playing with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4641-pebbles","name":"Pebbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T06:09:29-08:00","id":796799,"title":"","content":"I have a couple characters that i enjoyed naming mostly because their shadow names fit their character so nicely<br /> Verit - an FBI agent whose awakening happened in the midst of his agent exam. a Mastigos member of the 11th Question, seeking a sister only he believes to still be alive, and uses his FBI credentials to that end in his free time.<br /> Aria - a violin prodigy whose awakening involved her moving steadily toward a bright light that became so intense she clawed our her eyes and used the remains to sign her name on her Watchtower, thus leaving even Masters of Life unable to restore her sight. she passes herself off as an Obriomos with strong ties to Mind, but is actually a member of a hidden path she calls the Stygian path (optional lore that doesnt really change her much). she always carries her violin case with her, as she learned mudras associated with the fingerings she uses while she plays, and incorporates magic into her music, imbuing it with Emotional Urging and other spells. her bow and her cane are both dedicated items to act as wands for her casting. in the story she's in right now, she is actually responsible for the Chicago Fires due to being unable to exhibit full control at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1798-nameandverb","name":"NameAndVerb","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1798_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T08:02:31-08:00","id":796842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NameAndVerb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=796799#post796799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Verit - an FBI agent whose awakening happened in the midst of his agent exam. a Mastigos member of the 11th Question, seeking a sister only he believes to still be alive, and uses his FBI credentials to that end in his free time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fox Mulder so much... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T09:21:22-08:00","id":796861,"title":"","content":"I like Shadownames as part of the Persona the mage shows to other mages - it should be truthful (Prime arcana I\u00b4m looking at you!) enough that it is not an actual lie - like just a false name with no significance. symbolism is important - better so if it\u00b4s multilayered - that\u00b4s why the name of gods, spirits or literary characters are so powerful. <br /> <br /> In one of my stories i had a guardian who was mostly working for her order as a spy - she went by &quot;Sayeh&quot; (persian for: shadow, also her prefered magic). After her beloved cabal mate died, she left her cabal and named herself &quot;Tanha&quot; (persian for: alone). She also used a complete &quot;persian&quot; persona when she was among mages. <br /> <br /> I do not titles as names much as they are sometime quite cumbersome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T10:23:02-08:00","id":796887,"title":"","content":"A planned mage I have will have the shadow name sedah. He will be a mage focused on ghosts and finding a way to provide them with sanctuary. He will be the opposite of hades, not a jailer but a protector hence his shadow name simply being hades backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T11:00:53-08:00","id":796904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=796887#post796887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A planned mage I have will have the shadow name sedah. He will be a mage focused on ghosts and finding a way to provide them with sanctuary. He will be the opposite of hades, not a jailer but a protector hence his shadow name simply being hades backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.babynamespedia.com/meaning/Sedah\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.babynamespedia.com/meaning/Sedah</a><br /> <br /> Still works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T11:36:21-08:00","id":796924,"title":"","content":"A bitter, nihilistic, outcast mage with indelible Abyssal corruption assumed the name of his goth trance-metal group, Ho//owDoubt, both because he really <i>didn't </i>give a fuck any more and because the name was already Hollowed Out spelt sideways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 12-30-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T11:46:25-08:00","id":796927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=796904#post796904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://www.babynamespedia.com/meaning/Sedah\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.babynamespedia.com/meaning/Sedah</a><br /> <br /> Still works.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I know but that actual meaning to meant to disguise the intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:06:07-08:00","id":796935,"title":"","content":"I recently had a computer engineer Mystegos who joined the Transhumanist Engineers. Upon being initiated he took the shadow name Hopper in honor of Rear Admiral Grace Hopper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grace_Hopper\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Commodore_Grace_M._Hopper%2C_USN_%28covered%29_head_and_shoulders_crop.jpg/960px-Commodore_Grace_M._Hopper%2C_USN_%28covered%29_head_and_shoulders_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grace_Hopper\" target=\"_blank\"> Grace Hopper - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grace_Hopper\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grace_Hopper </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He uses a rune-scribed 1 foot long length of copper wire as his dedicated tool.<br /> <br /> I got to hear her speak once as a teen and she was simple an amazing women, I was really glad I was able to pay her a little honor in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","user":"ckobbe","date":". 12-30-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:36:47-08:00","id":796958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=796784#post796784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh he is pretty antagonistic sure, in both small and big things. Like not washing his hands before saluting a Mage with a terrible OCD, to showing up uninvited inside a sanctum wher other mages though they were hunted by Banishers (just to show them how unsafe they actually were), etc. If you are asking if it has a positive impact on others, well... Who knows. He won't admit doing it to help anyone. And people who are eventually helped don't admit that it was thanks to his intervention because he is just too disgusting and generally antinomian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:33:55-08:00","id":797165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=796778#post796778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And not a reference to Tom Sawyer?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, both the song and the character are Tom Sawyer references, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T23:11:10-08:00","id":797210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=795454#post795454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Adversary: A Mastigos Councilor that does his best to antagonize literally everyone just to cause them existential doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div>This NPC idea reminds me about <b>Diavolo</b> ( Devil ) from our Venice Chronicle, years ago. He was Mastigos Adamantine Sage and Consilior, that was ruling mafia family in Venice. He was slightly antagonists to all Ruling Council members, and even he's own Order Caucus - believing that internal conflict is strengthening all organisations. Fe was member of some Ceasares (?) Fan Legacy ( it was on first WW forum but cannot remember correct name now ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-16-2016, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T01:45:28-08:00","id":797235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=797165#post797165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWell, both the song and the character are Tom Sawyer references, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>I just find it funny you're referencing two separate references rather than just referencing the original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T02:02:51-08:00","id":797242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=796958#post796958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh he is pretty antagonistic sure, in both small and big things. Like not washing his hands before saluting a Mage with a terrible OCD, to showing up uninvited inside a sanctum wher other mages though they were hunted by Banishers (just to show them how unsafe they actually were), etc. If you are asking if it has a positive impact on others, well...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. It's just if you call yourself 'The Adversary' and go around being confrontational; then I could see a lot of magi simply tuning him out. He's just that guy who no one likes; which is pretty bad for his overall plan.<br /> <br /> Just curious how you played it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T07:26:18-08:00","id":797339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=797242#post797242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly. It's just if you call yourself 'The Adversary' and go around being confrontational; then I could see a lot of magi simply tuning him out. He's just that guy who no one likes; which is pretty bad for his overall plan.<br /> <br /> Just curious how you played it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, a lot of Mages really did go around trying to ignore his antics and avoided talking to him at all. There were a few problems though:<ul><li>He has a seat on the Ruling Council and had not Provost, while every other Councilor did, so he was technically the more approachable of them.</li> <li>He was really good at undetected Mind reading AND faking Mind reading (reading you through other clues) and used this to insert himself into your narrative, where he would offer help at a cost, and although most refuse (precisely because they already know who this is) some, specially the more inexperienced Disciples, usually had little choice.</li> <li>Sometimes he would seek you out in public places while he himself remained invisible to Sleepers and, after doing some legwork on his own about your Mysteries and the enemies besieging you, gave unrequested warnings. Mages who failed to heed them often ran into situations with a risk of Wisdom loss. Mages who listened to him often had the benefit of being resolute in their decision before coming to this risky situation, or avoiding it entirely although that almost always made the original worse (thus you kept your Wisdom, but the world went just a little darker).</li> <li>Other Masters think he isn't so bad of a Mentor, but then again, he is not interested in dealing with the big Masters either, his thing is harrasing the newbies. Because of this, the other Masters completely ignore him and never deal with him except on Council meetings and don't care much if the Disciples complain.</li> <li>Rumors say he used to be the Interfector when he was younger (some say he was only deployed once), and is the mentor of the current Interfector.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T15:56:58-08:00","id":797540,"title":"","content":"My preference for shadow names has shifted over the years, from the more punchy, thematic or 'superhero' like titles to something that a mage can use as a cover identity and give to a hotel clerk without too much of a problem, even if they seem like obvious fake names. My thinking is that if you've got a shadow name, you're going to need to use it for extended periods of time because there's all manner of different ways to perceive, detect, trace or connect a person with magic through time, fate, interconnections, etc. It wouldn't do to leave a place where you've been performing magic and going around calling yourself &quot;Nightbane&quot;, only to have someone follow your resonant traces through Time back to your apartment later that night, where you're getting mail as Dave Johnson. At the very least, you'd want to call yourself &quot;John Nightbane&quot; so you can get a driver's license or rent a motel room in town after you've spent the day throwing around perceiving and knowing spells, even if you also get a few stares or eyebrow raises. And maybe you're just NIghtbane to your wizard friends, but when you make a dinner reservation they might think it's a prank.<br /> <br /> I feel like operating as a mage would have to be like the most extreme version of going deep undercover in enemy territory, if you really cared about your name or true identity being used sympathetically, or enemy mages. As a mage, you're going to do some interacting with the mundane world. It would be unavoidable. And if you're going to be in the mundane world doing things, you're going to want a name you can drop there.<br /> <br /> The example in the Mage 1e core under Shadow Names seems reasonable in that sense: Glorianna. Some Sleeper asks for your name, you just tack a 'Smith' onto that and you're good to go. &quot;The Adversary&quot;, though... how would you get anything done in a day? You'd be acting through intermediaries or using magic for everything. Seems a bit excessive when you could pick a name that could &quot;pass&quot; at least a little in Sleeper society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10592-phlox","name":"Phlox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T18:47:10-08:00","id":797582,"title":"","content":"I do see your point, but I think it depends on mage style - some are going to want to go by a name like Adversary in mage society and an innocuous <i>fake</i> name in Sleeper society. Depends how much of a Sleeper presence they want and how separate they want it to be to Mage-life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T19:22:03-08:00","id":797598,"title":"","content":"IMHO, the best ones sound like stripper stage names. Plausible but clearly fake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T19:37:08-08:00","id":797607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=797235#post797235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just find it funny you're referencing two separate references rather than just referencing the original.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat was intentional, the 2 references are for different reasons; the character on &quot;Lost&quot; is a con-man, there's a line in the song about &quot;the SPACE he invades&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 12-31-2015, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T20:09:15-08:00","id":797624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=797598#post797598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, the best ones sound like stripper stage names. Plausible but clearly fake.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my Chicago game, a Thyrsus ex-Stripper (and illegitimate daughter of the Hierarch) calls herself Nevaeh, which was one of her stage names (The other choice was Cashmere)<br /> My own street-racing auto-mechanic/courier Moros (who loves Matter way more than Death) is called Redline, or 'Red' in mixed company.<br /> Red's stepsister is a half-Japanese Obrimos who took the name Kodachi (&quot;small sword&quot;) because she considers herself to be her cabal's back-up weapon.<br /> We've got a 7-foot Russian carnival sideshow/bareknuckle fighter turned Acanthus named Chernobyl, though he also goes by Mikhail (also not his true name).<br /> A Native American Moros bodyguard for the Silver Ladder named Strongarm, though he passes it off as a surname to Sleepers (&quot;John Strongarm&quot;).<br /> A 20-year-old Moros who has a lot of Space and uses it more than his ruling arcana. He came to the game without a proper shadow-name, but Kodachi dubbed him Jumper, and it stuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T05:52:15-08:00","id":797760,"title":"","content":"Some Mages have the Fame merit. They can have Shadow Names that are as crazy as they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:08:05-08:00","id":804345,"title":"","content":"I plan to make a Logophages Legacy ( from <b>Legacies: The Ancient</b> ) cabal in mine London chronicle that eat all traces of their memory in people around them so they, for the Pentacle society, <b><i>they do not exist</i></b>. They \u201cfeed\u201d on security breaches and need to purge memories of Pentacle from any traces of Intruders, like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/706212-intruder-yellow-sign-hallows-as-stars?p=710293#post710293\">Yellow Sign</a>. I do not have good Shadow Names for them, especially as wanted them to connect their NEW Shadow Names ( those from Logophages Personas ) to Britain's problems in last 40 years. In truth, they are continuing traditions of London's secret Logophages cabal from the time of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Fire_of_London\" target=\"_blank\">Great Fire of London</a>.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Leader of the group, Acanthus from Guardians of the Veil, that started this cabal in 80s, after being instruceted by last Logophages of WW2 and Cold War era. Name should reflect rising paranoia in Britain after 1984 Heathrow and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brighton_hotel_bombing#Attitudes_towards_security\" target=\"_blank\">Brighton hotel bombings</a>.</li> <li>His male student, Mastigos from Guardians of Veil, inducted after the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1993_Bishopsgate_bombing\" target=\"_blank\">Bishopsgate bombing in 1993</a>.</li> <li>Ex-Mysterium female Acanthus Ex-Censor that were inducted in 1997 to Legacy when she uncovered that Yellow Sign Intruder is coming in times of great turmoil, when people too much time spend rembering it and looking in to stars. With coming of millenium return the fashion on new weird ( with reading <i>King in Yellow</i> play ) and rise of Hallows numbers in the London made it almost dangerous breach of Yellow Sign. She saved Consillium by stealing all the books and evidence of it from Censorium, making sure Yellow Sign will not come back. ( At least it's what she thought she's done... )</li> <li>Moros from Guardians of Veil, who was part of one <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/7_July_2005_London_bombings\" target=\"_blank\">7/7/2005 bombings</a> \u2013 he survived, but seen dozen of people die and few dozen injured. The presise memories hunted him so much, he wanted to get rid of them \u2013 and he done when Logophages found him.</li> <li>Obrimos (think also about Mastigos, didn\u2019t decided ) female Guardian who is hacker to cleaning the cyber-security breaches after more and more prominent use of Internet and e-mails in memories exchange. She would join the group after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_UK_terrorist_incidents\" target=\"_blank\">2007 bomb threats</a>, that spanned paranoia in London and UK.</li> </ol>So what cool Shadow Names can you come up for them? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-09-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:45:23-08:00","id":804422,"title":"","content":"If they don't exist as far as anyone knows then they don't need names. They should stick to the Gaurdian tradition of wearing interchangeable masks that they switch frequently and never give a name to the PCs. They might have signals or numbers they use to identify themselves to each other, but they would regularly change those as well and eat the memories of past I.D.s to maintain their secrecy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-09-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T07:05:57-08:00","id":804429,"title":"","content":"I definitely don't know enough British/English/London history to help from that point of view, but 4 of the 5 have clear links to bombing incidents. Since it sounds like Mage2E will allow some sort of Yantra merit based around Shadow Name / Cabal identity, it might be worth pursuing something thematically linked.<br /> <br /> I would tread carefully, especially since these are real world tragedies that affected real people, but in a world of darkness I could see each of the bombings actually being frame of jobs, with the attacks actually being being something along the lines of extreme actions taken to destroy Abyssal intrusions. The bombers could be patsies for the actions of extremest mages preventing even worse tragedies. In a case like that the bombings could be seen a symbolically cleansing and erasing that which cannot be known, which might feed into the themes of the cabal. In that case taking the bombers names as Shadow Names might fit. It also lends it self to some pretty extreme modus operanti for the cabal as villians.<br /> <br /> I would just caution that something like this should be used cautiously cause it has real potential to offend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:19:18-08:00","id":804463,"title":"","content":"Sounds a bit like a mix of the Silence from Doctor Who and the Society of the Blind Eye from Gravity Falls...except tied more to paranoia and tragedy?<br /> <br /> I can take a stab at it:<br /> 1. Reminder<br /> 2. Pacem (short for Pacem Para Bellum)<br /> 3. Redactia <br /> 4. Shadow Ash<br /> 5. Wire<br /> <br /> I figure the shadow names for this group should be something seemingly innocuous to anyone outside the cabal, but personally relate back to the events that shaped and led them to come together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","user":"Knowbody","date":". 01-09-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:01:20-08:00","id":804489,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answers - I will just stick to this direct pointing Shadow Names.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=804463#post804463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Reminder<br /> 2. Pacem (short for Pacem Para Bellum)<br /> 3. Redactia<br /> 4. Shadow Ash<br /> 5. Wire<br /> <br /> I figure the shadow names for this group should be something seemingly innocuous to anyone outside the cabal, but personally relate back to the events that shaped and led them to come together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to translate them in to Polish for mine players, so I will ask on definitions or explanation on them:<br /> <br /> 1. Like &quot;notifications&quot; or like &quot;alarm clock&quot;?<br /> 2. The &quot;Peace&quot; from Latin, I get it.<br /> 3. Good one, on ex-Censor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 4. Do not understand this? What does name &quot;Ashley&quot; have to do this?<br /> 5. Like &quot;cable&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:56:27-08:00","id":804513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=804345#post804345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Leader of the group, Acanthus from Guardians of the Veil, that started this cabal in 80s, after being instruceted by last Logophages of WW2 and Cold War era. Name should reflect rising paranoia in Britain after 1984 Heathrow and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brighton_hotel_bombing#Attitudes_towards_security\" target=\"_blank\">Brighton hotel bombings</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about The Enemy Within? It's one of Margaret Thatcher's iconic phrases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T18:31:09-08:00","id":804892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=804463#post804463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds a bit like a mix of the Silence from Doctor Who and the Society of the Blind Eye from Gravity Falls...except tied more to paranoia and tragedy?<br /> <br /> I can take a stab at it:<br /> 1. Reminder<br /> 2. Pacem (short for Pacem Para Bellum)<br /> 3. Redactia<br /> 4. Shadow Ash<br /> 5. Wire<br /> <br /> I figure the shadow names for this group should be something seemingly innocuous to anyone outside the cabal, but personally relate back to the events that shaped and led them to come together.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRunning with that theme, might I suggest :<br /> <br /> 6. Retcon<br /> 7. Memento (probably a Moros)<br /> 8. Mnemosyne<br /> 9. Tabula Rasa (Rasa for short)<br /> 10. Lacuna<br /> 11, Omerta<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T02:36:25-08:00","id":805095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=804345#post804345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obrimos (think also about Mastigos, didn\u2019t decided ) female Guardian who is hacker to cleaning the cyber-security breaches after more and more prominent use of Internet and e-mails in memories exchange. She would join the group after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_UK_terrorist_incidents\" target=\"_blank\">2007 bomb threats</a>, that spanned paranoia in London and UK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered the using the 2008 Financial Crisis? You've set your game in one of the centres of global finance and it led to a genuine wave of paranoia and fear that continues to resonate down to the present day.<br /> <br /> In contrast, the trouble with the threats in 2007 is that they weren't terribly scary. The attack on Glasgow especially was a total joke. More broadly, in terms of crisis moments, it's one of the least plausible moments. There was a lot of talk at the time of the prime minister Gordon Brown holding a snap election because things were going so well and crisis-free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T02:46:06-08:00","id":805098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=804489#post804489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Do not understand this? What does name &quot;Ashley&quot; have to do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ash is what's left after something is burned in a fire, possibly a reference to them surviving the bombings. In Polish it should be 'popi\u00f3\u0142' I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T05:01:51-08:00","id":808586,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the names, everyone. Special thanks for the <b>Micheal</b> and <b>Michael</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I work now over my Legacies \u2013 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy\">Children of Stars</a> \u2013 cult-coven based in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Observatory,_Greenwich\" target=\"_blank\">Royal Greenwich Observatory</a>. Just as the Legacy at large they are outsiders to main London Consilium, leaving to be in the cellars under the hill. They are all cooperating with in to coming of Yellow Sign to the London now. Here are NPCs concepts I need Shadow Names for.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Acanthus of Free Council, leader of the coven and 40-something female astronomer by day and New Age astrologer by night. She was raised as white British in London, but went to New York for studies. She return to London in 2002, to take over her post in the Observatory and started Children\u2019s coven here \u2013 members joined in few next years, with last added in 2011. Rather reasonable demeanour, but truly fixated on the \u201ccosmic\u201d aspect of the Legacy. She was convinced by the rest to dwell in to Yellow Sign phenomena.</li> <li>Obrimos of Free Council, 30-something British male s-f horror writer, the UFO conspiracy theorist in reality. He said he was \u201ctaken\u201d at age of 19 and from them on he tries to remember all the details of his abduction, in way to solve how to be with aliens once more \u2013 in reality, it was his Awakening. He sees Children of the Stars on quasi spiritual level, trying to piece the elements need for the Second Contact. He thinks the Yellow Sign is a way to bring Them here, to commune with rest of Children.</li> <li>Obrimos of Free Council, 30-something black female archaeologist, Libertine archeomancer. When making her studies on Temples of Time Before she discovered that dating is impossible and Awaken by this fact. Joined Children because she feverously disapproves Atlantis Myth, seeing there is all more to the Truth. As Obrimos historian, she is curious how Hallows can develop in to the same star clusters now \u2013 and she wants to see what, in reality, is King in Yellow.</li> <li>Thyrsus of Free Council, 30-something white transvestite fringe evolutionist. He likes to walk as women for a few hours a day, but most of time he still thinks himself as more male persona \u2013 rather fluid, in the end. He believes that genders are putted on humanity by Exarchs as part of Sleeping Cures. First Ones created humanity as genderless, just like modern UFO myths describes \u201c<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey_alien\" target=\"_blank\">Grays</a>\u201d. He want to found where this happened, exactly, to try to revert this \u2013 at least for those that feel alien in their bodies. He spoke with some Planetary Spirits of Solar System and they sound to concur his theories. Yellow Sign, to him, could be validation of those theories and key to final understanding.</li> </ol>Someone will take a challenge on Shadow Names for those NPCs? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:27:04-08:00","id":809239,"title":"","content":"I've attempted, where possible, to translate the name into Polish although that really is a best guess since I don't speak Polish.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Precession (Precesja): </b>This is the name of the slow change to how the Earth spins, so that where the stars are in the sky changes very gradually over the years. (This ties in Time as an Acanthus to her interest in astronomy). Also Precession slowly changes what star signs are born in what month, so it can be viewed as a symbol for changing Fate.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Thumb (Kciuk):</b> This is a reference to the way a hitch-hiker (autostopowicz) shows that they want a car to stop and pick them in. In this case it's a reference to wanting the Aliens to stop and pick him up again.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Patterson (Patterson):</b> This is a reference to Clair Cameron Patterson, a scientist who produced one of the most accurate measures of the age of the Earth, however he had a lot of trouble calculating this due to human pollution altering the results. This is a reference to her Awakening and belief that the rest of Mage society is blind to the way they're hiding the reality of the past.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Iphis (Iphis):</b> This is a reference to Iphis, the Daughter of Ligdus, a character from the Roman poet Ovid's Metamorphoses. Iphis was born a girl, but grew up disguised as a boy by her mother. This was to stop the father from killing the child because they couldn't afford a daughter's dowry. When Iphis falls in love with another woman, she prays to the Gods who physically transform her into a man to allow them to get married.<br /> <br /> Those are a couple of ideas, hopefully they might help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T00:16:31-08:00","id":809410,"title":"","content":"Great ideas <b>Michael </b>- I probably use all of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Well, on 2 I'm not sure, but rest are great!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=809239#post809239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've attempted, where possible, to translate the name into Polish although that really is a best guess since I don't speak Polish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not sweat on it - if you only use Google Translate to write in Polish, best to not use it. Translate is good for quick finding term, but for the precise or complex translation better to use proper dictionaries or even go with &quot;language hunch&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For this topic all you put as &quot;arguments&quot; behind the English Name and description is all that is needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=809239#post809239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. <b>Precession (Precesja): </b>This is the name of the slow change to how the Earth spins, so that where the stars are in the sky changes very gradually over the years. (This ties in Time as an Acanthus to her interest in astronomy). Also Precession slowly changes what star signs are born in what month, so it can be viewed as a symbol for changing Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also have interesting connotation in Polish, that is similar to English Pilgrimage ( like in <b>Promethean</b> ) - so maybe I will add a nice touch on her story that she roamed few Consilia before returning to London, always looking for her place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=809239#post809239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. <b>Thumb (Kciuk):</b> This is a reference to the way a hitch-hiker (autostopowicz) shows that they want a car to stop and pick them in. In this case it's a reference to wanting the Aliens to stop and pick him up again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the idea behind this, but I'm not sure is fitting name for one that see himself as s-f writer and aliens priest in one. Something not working in mine head for this Shadow Name idea, sounding to pulpy probably. Maybe someone has another?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=809239#post809239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. <b>Patterson (Patterson):</b> This is a reference to Clair Cameron Patterson, a scientist who produced one of the most accurate measures of the age of the Earth, however he had a lot of trouble calculating this due to human pollution altering the results. This is a reference to her Awakening and belief that the rest of Mage society is blind to the way they're hiding the reality of the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great! I will read on her before the play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=809239#post809239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. <b>Iphis (Iphis):</b> This is a reference to Iphis, the Daughter of Ligdus, a character from the Roman poet Ovid's Metamorphoses. Iphis was born a girl, but grew up disguised as a boy by her mother. This was to stop the father from killing the child because they couldn't afford a daughter's dowry. When Iphis falls in love with another woman, she prays to the Gods who physically transform her into a man to allow them to get married.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really spot on - I thought I would need to dwell in some Celtic or even Asian mythology, when I think most British mages rather stick to the Greek or Roman mythology. Will dwell in to Iphis more preparing for next play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T04:45:56-08:00","id":809504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=808586#post808586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Obrimos of Free Council, 30-something British male s-f horror writer, the UFO conspiracy theorist in reality. He said he was \u201ctaken\u201d at age of 19 and from them on he tries to remember all the details of his abduction, in way to solve how to be with aliens once more \u2013 in reality, it was his Awakening. He sees Children of the Stars on quasi spiritual level, trying to piece the elements need for the Second Contact. He thinks the Yellow Sign is a way to bring Them here, to commune with rest of Children.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about Hastur? If he's mixing up the Yellow Sign with his Awakening, then perhaps he thinks that's the name of the alien who abducted him. Naming yourself after them would be quite appropriate.<br /> <br /> 'Course, that tips your hand to the audience that bad things are afoot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:07:31-08:00","id":809630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names?p=809504#post809504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Hastur? If he's mixing up the Yellow Sign with his Awakening, then perhaps he thinks that's the name of the alien who abducted him. Naming yourself after them would be quite appropriate.<br /> <br /> 'Course, that tips your hand to the audience that bad things are afoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not say his name three times? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's intriguing, will probably go with it if no one propose anything other. It's a bit illogical as I have literal <i>Logophagens</i> cabal to eat any hints of Yellow Sign in London area, so they should eat any idea a loud Obrimos like this would have - but it also nice touch that coming of King in Yellow was prophesied by one Libertine Awakening...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-15-2016, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T02:18:25-08:00","id":810148,"title":"","content":"Well, if they've done a good enough job, how do they know what to look for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T03:12:12-08:00","id":810160,"title":"","content":"Went with Hastur name, but changed Path to Mastigos for character - it sounds more fitting. Added one PC's mentor as fifth NPC, some details changed in descriptions. If interested - final version of Children's coven is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=810157#post810157\">here</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T17:16:11-08:00","id":810881,"title":"","content":"I had a player once who played this girl who was really brash, cocky, and flippant. When she was told that she needed to pick a shadow name, she decided to intentionally go with the dumbest thing she could think of to take the piss out of the entire affair.<br /> <br /> For context, this character was a tiny, Japanese girl<br /> <br /> Her shadow name was Mai<br /> <br /> Mai Waifu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:58:53-08:00","id":810927,"title":"","content":"I played a Free Councilor who called herself Anarchy (her online handle was a L337 speek version of Little Orphan Anarchy). She had a problem with authority and since this was in a play by post sandbox game, there were a lot of people trying to establish themselves as authority figures. I think the local Syndic (who was also technically a Thyrsus) thought she was actually literally insane, because she didn't like his high handed and bossy attitude.<br /> <br /> She was a rough character, she burned me out and as a result I didn't leave that game on good terms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T16:58:53-08:00","id":811386,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <br /> Longa est quod nemo unquam dicere vellent sum ita quod in me ipsum<br /> I just used google translate for it and it pretty much means (I assume). this is a really long word that no one will ever say so that's why chose it I'm so smart","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T06:11:27-07:00","id":924860,"title":"","content":"For my London setting I need Shadow Name for the Mysterium researcher on High Speech and Vinca people ( yes, like civilization from <i>Sundered World</i> chapter in <b>Dark Eras</b> book. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T07:13:15-07:00","id":924872,"title":"","content":"Omphalos?<br /> <br /> It's both the archeaological term for the Vinca Omphalos stones, and the place in the Astral related to High Speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T10:06:35-07:00","id":924924,"title":"","content":"<b>Ba'al Anansi </b>- Magistos - Clavicularius - Silver Ladder<br /> Spiders, Stories, strands, stealing, sneaking, spider webbing<br /> Nimus: All shadows are roiling masses of spiders, connections between people are spidewebbing, if you get forces/prime gospel choir repeats his words for emphasis<br /> Telling a story in the third person for emotional urging<br /> Reading a mind as stealing a story<br /> Stealing stories from the world's story to summon his vices as Goetia<br /> Can do weaving or knitting as a yantra<br /> <br /> Lust Hitch<br /> Pride Kanye West<br /> Envy Aaron Burr from that Hamilton musical<br /> Sloth Snoop Dogg<br /> Wrath Black Dynamite<br /> Greed Stringer Bell<br /> Gluttony ODB","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11776-neotoma","name":"Neotoma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T14:33:13-07:00","id":925049,"title":"","content":"I made an Moros Forge Master Guardian of the Veil who took Abraxas for his Shadow Name due to its significance in Gnostic philosophy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the system described by <i>Irenaeus</i>, &quot;the Unbegotten Father&quot; is the progenitor of <i>Nous</i>, and from <i>Nous Logos</i>, from <i>Logos Phronesis</i>, from <i>Phronesis Sophia</i> and <i>Dynamis</i>, from <i>Sophia</i> and <i>Dynamis</i> principalities, powers, and angels, the last of whom create &quot;the first heaven.&quot; They in turn originate a second series, who create a second heaven. The process continues in like manner until 365 heavens are in existence, the angels of the last or visible heaven being the authors of our world. &quot;The ruler&quot; [<i>principem, i.e.</i>, probably <i>ton archonta</i>] of the 365 heavens &quot;is Abraxas, and for this reason he contains within himself 365 numbers.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Taking the name of a being that was responsible for the creation of the Heavens and the Earth is a pretty awesome name for a Forge Master, wouldn't you say?<br /> <br /> Also, the name appears in Simon R. Green's Nightside series, where there is an inscription upon the stock of the Speaking Gun, which unmakes people by speaking their True Name backwards. The inscription reads;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abraxus Artificers, the old firm. Solving problems since the beginning. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":1220,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","user":"CarnivalCash","date":". 07-02-2016, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:13:18-07:00","id":925115,"title":"","content":"Pollinating our Mage game set in the Consilia of Manila has been fun and challenging. The Shadow Names are diverse, and borrow from colorful Filipino folklore, pagan mythology, and history. The PCs are:<br /> <br /> Alunsina, a Mastigos blogger, socialite, and saboteur. Alunsina was a beauty goddess in ancient Visayan religion.<br /> <br /> Mumbaki, an Ifugao Obrimos apostate obsessed with angelology. It means 'sayer of prayers ' in Ifugao culture.<br /> <br /> Cham, an Acanthus mixologist and vagabond-type. Cham is short for 'tsamba' which means 'lucky'.<br /> <br /> Pastilan, a Mastigos hacker and resident computers expert of the cabal. It's a Cebuano word for 'trouble-maker' and can also be said out of frustration similar to 'Darn it!'.<br /> <br /> Mage NPCs include:<br /> Mandragora the Thyrsus herbalist and poisons master who collects specimens from floral Atavisms.<br /> <br /> Orfeo the Acanthus susceptor who orchestrates Guardian activities from behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> Kankaraeg an 800-year old, mummified tribal sorcerer from the Philippine highlands.<br /> <br /> Terpsichore the Libertine Obrimos who performs with Ballet Philippines.<br /> <br /> Putla (Pale in Tagalog) a half-Filipino, half-American Arrow boxer ala Manny Pacquiao.<br /> <br /> Future names: Asymptote, Nebulos, Magdiwang (To celebrate), Sulayman, Darjeeling, Ephemera, Kudyapi (A native lute), Idiyanale (goddess of fruitful labor and good deeds), Libertad, Reyna Elena, Berdugo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:25:12-07:00","id":925378,"title":"","content":"The short story <u>Mana From Heaven</u> by Roger Zelazny, which took place in the &quot;present day&quot; of Larry Niven's Warlock Universe, used shadow names after a fashion. All of the mages derived their name from a mythological creature or cultural concept and their magical signatures reflected such. Think Phoenix (the first person protagonist), Dervish, Gnome, Werewolf, and so on. These mages were much fewer in number than those in an average Awakening game, I should note, making such general concepts less likely to collide with one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:27:31-07:00","id":992147,"title":"","content":"Any name from The Venture Bros. The Monarch, Phantom Limb, Dr. Orpheus, Vendata, Sergeant Hatred, Henchman 21, Radical Left, Monstroso, Night Dick..<br /> <br /> The Malfeasance Collective, a cabal of supervillains I came up with, is comprised of: The Abominable Dr. Cortex, Clock Lobster, Adam Pretorius XIII, Red Menace, Hallowitch, Super Dario, and The Veganator. They're all part of a Legacy of supervillains founded by Craniac The Undying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-23-2016, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}